{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>הנה יד ד׳ הויה.</b> We find that yod and vav interchange: ואתה הוה להם למלך (Nehemiah 6:6), and the reverse: the vav of שלא יבשו קוָֹי (Isaiah 49:23) interchanges with yod, וקוֵֹי ד׳ יחליפו כח (Isaiah 40:31)." "And the word דבר is a general noun; we do not find it among verbs except in one place: ותדבר את כל זרע המלוכה (II Chronicles 22:10), and in the book of Kings it is written ותאבד (II Kings 11:1). The explanation is far-fetched, but we do not know anything better than it."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:51.059714594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}